Select for charge, heat, light and magnetic response (@mat-functional-selection: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @materials-engineering, #source "../sources/Economic-and-Environmental-Materials-Selection-MIT.lingua#r_36KMERFT8SDRP30MT63KQ5WS6C", #source "../sources/Sustainable-Materials-Selection-DOE.lingua#r_04ADQ1BN156GM7AVH5N2T7EAJZ", #materials-engineering "Interfaces-and-layered-materials-in-selection.lingua#r_61JDZQS4Q2VX4BZN2AS34CR3EW") { r_5KWWMHA5TV3SJJNT08MTH6TGQ0
**Read:** Revisit the complete functional-properties sequence and its sources; [Economic and environmental issues in materials selection — MIT 3.080](../sources/Economic-and-Environmental-Materials-Selection-MIT.lingua#r_36KMERFT8SDRP30MT63KQ5WS6C), selection methods; [Sustainable Materials Selection in Manufactured Products — DOE, 2023](../sources/Sustainable-Materials-Selection-DOE.lingua#r_04ADQ1BN156GM7AVH5N2T7EAJZ), insulation case.

For a uniform electrical conductor of fixed length L, resistance R=L/(σA) and mass ρAL give a mass index σ/ρ under a resistance constraint. For a plane insulation layer at fixed area and required thermal resistance per area R″=t/k, mass per area is ρkR″. Minimizing it favors small ρk, provided thickness, radiation, moisture, temperature and mechanical constraints are also satisfied. The two functions require different transport behavior.

Optical transmission requires a wavelength and thickness; a magnetic comparison requires field history and frequency. Dielectric loss, thermal expansion, contact resistance and environmental stability may govern useful performance even when a bulk conductivity or permeability appears favorable.

**Work:** Derive the conductor and insulation relations and challenge their assumptions. Compare two complete material states for an optical window, electrical contact or magnetic component using frequency/temperature-dependent evidence. Include a constraint from another physical field and explain why a single scalar property cannot represent the complete choice.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
